You can focus on an element found by `getElementsByTagName` using JavaScript by using the `focus()` method on the element.

Here is an example:
```
var elements = document.getElementsByTagName('input');
elements[0].focus(); // focus on the first input element
```
This will focus on the first `input` element in the document.

If you want to focus on a specific element, you can use the `getId` method to get the element by its ID, or you can use a loop to iterate over the elements and find the one you want to focus on.

For example:
```
var element = document.getElementById('myInput');
element.focus(); // focus on the element with ID "myInput"

// or

var elements = document.getElementsByTagName('input');
for (var i = 0; i < elements.length; i++) {
  if (elements[i].getAttribute('name') === 'myInputName') {
    elements[i].focus(); // focus on the input element with name "myInputName"
  }
}
```
